IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `whs-worker`
IMPORT `whs-seat-pcbu`
IMPORT `whs-penalty-indexation`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 -- worked cases for the Schedule 4 indexation (cls 4, 5, 7), from the worker's seat and
-- the PCBU's.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand
-- from Schedule 4 of the deposited text (C2024C00243) and the cl 4(2) formula in C2011A00137.formulas.md, A × (B / C), never
-- copied from the encoding's output.
--
-- THE CPI NUMBERS ARE HYPOTHETICAL. None is deposited, so every case uses made-up index numbers chosen to make the
-- arithmetic plain and to reach each rounding rule: C (March quarter 2022) = 120 throughout, and B = 132 (A × 1.1),
-- 135 (A × 1.125), 129 (A × 1.075, a fall), 138 (A × 1.15), 114 (A × 0.95, below C), 144 (A × 1.2), 133 and 135.1.
-- The figures below are therefore not the penalties in force in any year.
--
-- Priya (whs-cases-worker.l4) and Northline Logistics Pty Ltd (whs-cases-pcbu.l4), both HYPOTHETICAL, ask the penalty
-- questions again with the fines indexed. There are no mirror cases: the worker and the business are in different
-- columns of cl 1, so the same facts give each a different figure.

§ `cases`

§§ `cl 7 -- the year`

-- A year runs from 1 July; it is named by the calendar year it starts in.
#ASSERT `the Schedule 4 year that includes` (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS 2024
#ASSERT `the Schedule 4 year that includes` (Date 1 7 2025) EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT `the Schedule 4 year that includes` (Date 1 7 2024) EQUALS 2024
#ASSERT `the Schedule 4 year that includes` (Date 30 6 2024) EQUALS 2023

§§ `cl 5 -- rounding`

-- More than $10,000: to the nearest $1,000, with $500 rounded down.
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 229900 EQUALS 230000
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 31500 EQUALS 31000
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 15500.5 EQUALS 16000
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 15400 EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 77000 EQUALS 77000
-- Just over $10,000 goes to the nearest $1,000 under para (b), not to the nearest $100: $10,080 is $10,000.
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 10080 EQUALS 10000
-- Exactly $10,000: in neither paragraph, and a multiple of both.
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 10000 EQUALS 10000
-- Less than $10,000: to the nearest $100, with $50 rounded down; a cent above $50 goes up.
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 9450 EQUALS 9400
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 9450.25 EQUALS 9500
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 9451 EQUALS 9500
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 9996 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `rounded under cl 5` 1870 EQUALS 1900

§§ `cl 4(2), (3) -- one year`

-- 209,000 × 129 / 120 = 224,675, less than the $230,000 that applied the year before: $230,000 continues (cl 4(3)).
#ASSERT `the amount applying in the year` 209000 129 120 230000 EQUALS 230000
-- 209,000 × 138 / 120 = 240,350, not less than $230,000: rounded, $240,000.
#ASSERT `the amount applying in the year` 209000 138 120 230000 EQUALS 240000
-- 209,000 × 114 / 120 = 198,550, less than the $209,000 set out: $209,000 continues.
#ASSERT `the amount applying in the year` 209000 114 120 209000 EQUALS 209000

§§ `ss 28, 31 to 34, Schedule 4 cls 1, 4, 5 -- Priya, a worker (column 3)`

-- 2024-25 (a day in September 2024), B = 132: category 1 $1,500,000 × 1.1 = $1,650,000, a multiple of $1,000; 15 years
-- unchanged. Category 2 $209,000 × 1.1 = $229,900, to $230,000. Category 3 $70,000 × 1.1 = $77,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 1: negligent or reckless conduct, without reasonable excuse, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 31)` (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 1650000, 15)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 230000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)` (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 77000, 0)
-- Industrial manslaughter is not open against a worker as such (s 30A(1)(a)), as in whs-worker.l4.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `industrial manslaughter: intentional conduct breaching a health and safety duty that causes a death, reckless or negligent as to it (s 30A)` (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS `no such offence for this offender`

-- 2024-25 (15 March 2025), B = 135: category 1 $1,500,000 × 1.125 = $1,687,500; $500 is rounded down, $1,687,000.
-- Category 2 $209,000 × 1.125 = $235,125, to $235,000. Category 3 $70,000 × 1.125 = $78,750, to $79,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 1: negligent or reckless conduct, without reasonable excuse, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 31)` (Date 15 3 2025) 120 (LIST 135) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 1687000, 15)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` (Date 15 3 2025) 120 (LIST 135) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 235000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)` (Date 15 3 2025) 120 (LIST 135) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 79000, 0)
-- B = 133: category 2 $209,000 × 133 / 120 = $231,641.67, to $232,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 133) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 232000, 0)

-- 2025-26 (1 August 2025), the March 2025 number falls to 129. Category 2: 2024-25 $230,000; 2025-26 $209,000 × 1.075 =
-- $224,675, less than $230,000, so $230,000 continues (cl 4(3)). Category 3: $77,000; then $75,250, so $77,000 continues.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` (Date 1 8 2025) 120 (LIST 132, 129) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2025, 230000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)` (Date 1 8 2025) 120 (LIST 132, 129) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2025, 77000, 0)

-- 2026-27 (1 July 2026), March 2026 = 138. Category 2 $209,000 × 1.15 = $240,350, to $240,000. Category 3 $70,000 × 1.15 =
-- $80,500; $500 is rounded down, $80,000. Category 1: $1,650,000; then $1,612,500 (kept at $1,650,000); then $1,725,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` (Date 1 7 2026) 120 (LIST 132, 129, 138) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2026, 240000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)` (Date 1 7 2026) 120 (LIST 132, 129, 138) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2026, 80000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 1: negligent or reckless conduct, without reasonable excuse, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 31)` (Date 1 7 2026) 120 (LIST 132, 129, 138) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2026, 1725000, 15)

-- The March 2024 number below the March 2022 one (114): $209,000 × 0.95 = $198,550, less than the $209,000 set out, which
-- is read as the amount that applied in 2023-24, so $209,000 continues (NOTES.md finding 18).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` (Date 1 7 2024) 120 (LIST 114) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 209000, 0)
-- B equal to C: the printed figure, as whs-worker.l4 gives it (whs-cases-worker.l4: category 1 $1,500,000 or 15 years).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 1: negligent or reckless conduct, without reasonable excuse, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 31)` (Date 1 7 2024) 120 (LIST 120) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 1500000, 15)
-- Only the numbers the year needs are used: September 2024 with three numbers given is the first one's figure.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132, 129, 138) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 230000, 0)

-- Not covered: a day before 1 July 2024; a year whose CPI numbers are not all given.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` (Date 30 6 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS `no indexed maximum` `the day is before 1 July 2024: cl 4(1) indexes from the year starting then, and the penalties before this compilation (1 July 2024) are not encoded`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` (Date 1 7 2025) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS `no indexed maximum` `a CPI number is missing: one is needed for the March quarter of each year from 2024 to the March quarter before the year asked about`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker, as indexed` `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)` (Date 1 9 2024) 120 EMPTY EQUALS `no indexed maximum` `a CPI number is missing: one is needed for the March quarter of each year from 2024 to the March quarter before the year asked about`

§§ `ss 30A to 33, Schedule 4 cls 1, 4, 5 -- Northline and its director (columns 2 and 4)`

-- Northline, a body corporate, 2024-25, B = 132: category 1 $15,000,000 × 1.1 = $16,500,000; category 2 $2,090,000 × 1.1 =
-- $2,299,000; category 3 $700,000 × 1.1 = $770,000. Industrial manslaughter: $18,000,000, set by s 30A, not indexed.
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `category 1: negligent or reckless conduct, without reasonable excuse, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 31)` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 16500000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 2299000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 770000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `industrial manslaughter: intentional conduct breaching a health and safety duty that causes a death, reckless or negligent as to it (s 30A)` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the s 30A maximum, which Schedule 4 does not index` OF 18000000, 0)
-- Its warehouse director, an officer: category 1 $3,000,000 × 1.1 = $3,300,000 or 15 years; category 2 $418,000 × 1.1 =
-- $459,800, to $460,000; category 3 $140,000 × 1.1 = $154,000; industrial manslaughter 25 years, from s 30A.
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `category 1: negligent or reckless conduct, without reasonable excuse, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 31)` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 3300000, 15)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 460000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 154000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `industrial manslaughter: intentional conduct breaching a health and safety duty that causes a death, reckless or negligent as to it (s 30A)` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the s 30A maximum, which Schedule 4 does not index` OF 0, 25)
-- s 30A needs no CPI number.
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `industrial manslaughter: intentional conduct breaching a health and safety duty that causes a death, reckless or negligent as to it (s 30A)` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 EMPTY EQUALS (`the s 30A maximum, which Schedule 4 does not index` OF 18000000, 0)
-- B below C (114): $700,000 × 0.95 = $665,000, less than $700,000, which continues.
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)` TRUE (Date 1 7 2024) 120 (LIST 114) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 700000, 0)
-- B equal to C: the printed figure, as whs-cases-pcbu.l4 gives it ($2,090,000).
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` TRUE (Date 1 7 2024) 120 (LIST 120) EQUALS (`the indexed maximum` OF 2024, 2090000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most the business can be fined, as indexed` `industrial manslaughter: intentional conduct breaching a health and safety duty that causes a death, reckless or negligent as to it (s 30A)` TRUE (Date 30 6 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS `no indexed maximum` `the day is before 1 July 2024: cl 4(1) indexes from the year starting then, and the penalties before this compilation (1 July 2024) are not encoded`

§§ `Schedule 4 cls 2, 3 -- the amounts set out`

-- The figures whs-seat-pcbu.l4's comments give, before indexation: tier D $14,000 / $70,000 (s 38(1)), tier F $7,000 /
-- $35,000 (s 38(7)). They agree.
#ASSERT `the amount set out in cl 2` `the tier D monetary penalty` FALSE EQUALS 14000
#ASSERT `the amount set out in cl 2` `the tier D monetary penalty` TRUE EQUALS 70000
#ASSERT `the amount set out in cl 2` `the tier F monetary penalty` FALSE EQUALS 7000
#ASSERT `the amount set out in cl 2` `the tier F monetary penalty` TRUE EQUALS 35000
#ASSERT `the amount set out in cl 2` `the tier I monetary penalty` TRUE EQUALS 8500
#ASSERT `the amount set out in cl 3` `the WHS civil penalty provision tier 1` FALSE EQUALS 28000
#ASSERT `the amount set out in cl 3` `the WHS civil penalty provision tier 4` TRUE EQUALS 14000

§§ `Schedule 4 cls 2, 4, 5 -- tier penalties, as indexed`

-- Northline does not ensure Comcare is notified (s 38(1), tier D), 2024-25, B = 132: $70,000 × 1.1 = $77,000. Its
-- director, an individual: $14,000 × 1.1 = $15,400, to $15,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier D monetary penalty` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 77000)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier D monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 15000)
-- Not consulting (s 47(1), tier C), an individual, B = 135: $28,000 × 1.125 = $31,500; $500 rounds down, $31,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier C monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 135) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 31000)
-- Tier E, an individual: B = 135, $8,400 × 1.125 = $9,450, $50 rounds down, $9,400; B = 135.1, $9,457, to $9,500;
-- B = 144, $10,080, over $10,000, so to the nearest $1,000: $10,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier E monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 135) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 9400)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier E monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 135.1) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 9500)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier E monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 144) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 10000)
-- Tier E, a body corporate, B = 132: $42,000 × 1.1 = $46,200, to $46,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier E monetary penalty` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 46000)
-- Tier I, B = 132: an individual $1,700 × 1.1 = $1,870, to $1,900; a body corporate $8,500 × 1.1 = $9,350, $50 rounds
-- down, $9,300. B = 133, an individual: $1,884.17, to $1,900.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier I monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 1900)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier I monetary penalty` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 9300)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier I monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 133) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 1900)
-- Not keeping the incident record (s 38(7), tier F), B = 132: an individual $7,000 × 1.1 = $7,700; a body corporate
-- $35,000 × 1.1 = $38,500, $500 rounds down, $38,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier F monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 7700)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier F monetary penalty` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 38000)
-- Tier A, B = 132: an individual $139,000 × 1.1 = $152,900, to $153,000; a body corporate $695,000 × 1.1 = $764,500, $500
-- rounds down, $764,000. Tier B, a body corporate: $385,000. Tier G, an individual: $5,500. Tier H, an individual:
-- $3,080, to $3,100.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier A monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 153000)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier A monetary penalty` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 764000)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier B monetary penalty` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 385000)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier G monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 5500)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier H monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 3100)
-- B equal to C: the amount set out.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier I monetary penalty` TRUE (Date 1 9 2024) 120 (LIST 120) EQUALS (`the indexed amount` OF 2024, 8500)
-- Before 1 July 2024: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined at a penalty tier, as indexed` `the tier D monetary penalty` FALSE (Date 30 6 2024) 120 (LIST 132) EQUALS `no indexed amount` `the day is before 1 July 2024: cl 4(1) indexes from the year starting then, and the penalties before this compilation (1 July 2024) are not encoded`

